## Phase 4 — Recovery (Frontend Reload / Reconnect)

**Actor:** Frontend (on page reload or app resume)

**Endpoint:** `GET /api/payments/order/:orderId/attempts`

```
Frontend reloads mid-payment
        │
        ▼
GET /api/payments/order/:orderId/attempts
        │
        ▼
Return order + all payment attempts (status, gatewayOrderId, etc.)
        │
        ▼
Frontend checks:
        ├─ Any attempt SUCCESS? → show success screen (Rule 7 — delayed success handled)
        ├─ Active PENDING attempt with gatewayOrderId?
        │       │
        │       └─ Frontend calls POST /api/payments/razorpay/order with SAME idempotencyKey
        │               │
        │               └─ Backend detects existing attempt → reconciles with Razorpay
        │                       ├─ Already captured → confirm + return success
        │                       └─ Still pending → return existing razorpayOrder → reopen Checkout
        │
        └─ All attempts FAILED/CANCELLED? → allow new attempt with new idempotencyKey
```

### Business Rules Enforced (Phase 4)
- ✅ **Rule 2** — All historical attempts visible in the response.
- ✅ **Rule 3** — Same idempotencyKey returns same attempt, never creates a duplicate.
- ✅ **Rule 4** — Active attempt detected → frontend cannot initiate a second one.
- ✅ **Rule 7** — If webhook arrived while frontend was away, success is detected here.

